  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A pressure-pump has a horizontal tube of cross-sectional area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math> for the outflow of water at a speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The force exerted on the vertical wall just in front of the tube which stops water horizontally flowing out of the tube, is: [given : density of water <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>]",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "3tQeq",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "gLAUV",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "IaAF8",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>250</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>",
